# onUpdate

`onUpdate` is called once per frame while any of a motion component's values
change. It receives every latest value on the element, not just the one that
changed.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { motion } from '@humanspeak/svelte-motion'

  let x = $state(0)
</script>

<motion.div
  animate={{ x: 100, opacity: 1 }}
  onUpdate={(latest) => (x = Number(latest.x))}
/>
```

<Example isSmall exampleUrl="/examples/on-update">
  <OnUpdateExample />
</Example>

## Callback Shape

```ts
type MotionOnUpdate = (latest: ResolvedValues) => void
```

- `latest` holds every current value on the element, keyed by name, for
  example `{ x: 42, rotate: 90, opacity: 0.5 }`.
- It runs at most once per frame, after values change and before they render,
  however many values changed that frame.

## Prop vs transition `onUpdate`

`onUpdate` can also go in a `transition`. The two are different:

```svelte
<!-- Prop: every value on the element, once per frame -->
<motion.div animate={{ x: 100, opacity: 1 }} onUpdate={(latest) => console.log(latest)} />

<!-- Transition: per animation, only that animation's value -->
<motion.div
  animate={{ x: 100 }}
  transition={{ duration: 1, onUpdate: (x) => console.log(x) }}
/>
```

The transition-level callback is called by each animation it applies to, with
that one value.

## Hardware acceleration

Having `onUpdate` keeps the element's transforms on the main thread, so only
use it when you need every frame. Since Motion 14.2, transform shortcuts like
`x`, `scale`, and `rotate` otherwise run as one hardware-accelerated animation
per element. Adding `onUpdate` while an accelerated animation is playing moves
it to the main thread. For a single value, prefer
[`useMotionValueEvent`](/docs/use-motion-value-event).
[`transformTemplate`](/docs/transform-template) has the same effect on
acceleration.

## API Reference

### `onUpdate`

```ts
onUpdate?: (latest: ResolvedValues) => void
```

Pass a callback to any `motion.*` component. The `MotionOnUpdate` type is
exported from `@humanspeak/svelte-motion`.

Based on [Motion's onUpdate prop](https://motion.dev/docs/react-motion-component#onupdate).
